{"id":2785,"age":47,"sex":"F","race":"Non-Hispanic White","insurance":"Employer-sponsored PPO","profile":{"sex":"F","allergies":["NKDA"],"insurance":"Employer-sponsored PPO","occupation":"Graphic designer","alcohol_use":"Occasional (1-2 drinks per month)","family_history":["Mother: Hashimoto thyroiditis","Maternal aunt: Rheumatoid arthritis"],"race_ethnicity":"Non-Hispanic White","smoking_status":"Never","home_medications":[],"surgical_history":[],"chronic_conditions":[],"age_at_first_encounter":47},"comorbidities_listed":[],"primary":{"did":4291,"code":"M33.10","name":"Dermatomyositis"},"filing":{"chapter":13,"block":"M30-M36","block_desc":"Systemic connective tissue disorders (M30-M36)"},"encounters":[{"id":11781,"date":"2020-01-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Dermatology","attending":"Dr. Sarah Chen","cc":"persistent rash on the dorsal surfaces of her hands","order":0,"method":"template","question_ids":[6844],"sections":[{"sid":54072,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Persistent rash on the dorsal surfaces of her hands"]},{"sid":54073,"type":"hpi","lines":["She presents for evaluation of a persistent rash on the dorsal surfaces of her hands that has developed over the past three weeks.","She reports mild muscle weakness, particularly when climbing stairs or rising from a chair, but denies joint pain or photosensitivity."]},{"sid":54074,"type":"pmh","lines":["She has no history of epilepsy, involuntary movements, or lipid disorders"]},{"sid":54075,"type":"medications","lines":["She has not started any new medications recently"]},{"sid":54076,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":54077,"type":"family_history","lines":["Her family history is unremarkable"]},{"sid":54078,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: Occasional (1-2 drinks per month). Occupation: Graphic designer."]},{"sid":54079,"type":"ros","lines":["Review of systems is negative for fever, hematuria, or chest pain"]},{"sid":54080,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Physical examination reveals violaceous, flat-topped papules overlying the metacarpophalangeal and interphalangeal joints.","She does not have any oral ulcers or discoid lesions, and there is no evidence of Raynaud phenomenon."]},{"sid":54081,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies reveal elevated creatine kinase and aldolase levels, while ANA is positive but anti-dsDNA and anti-Smith antibodies are negative."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11783,"date":"2020-02-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Rheumatology","attending":"Dr. Michael Rodriguez","cc":"progressive fatigue and worsening difficulty performing daily tasks over the past 3 months","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[6839],"sections":[{"sid":54082,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressive fatigue and worsening difficulty performing daily tasks over the past 3 months"]},{"sid":54083,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns for rheumatology evaluation approximately one month following her initial dermatology presentation for persistent rash on the dorsal surfaces of her hands.","She presents with progressive fatigue and worsening difficulty performing daily tasks over the past three months.","She reports that she has been struggling to lift her arms above her head to wash her hair and has had increasing trouble rising from chairs or climbing stairs.","She also notes the development of a scaly, reddish rash on the backs of her hands and a pinkish-purple discoloration of her eyelids that she initially thought was related to makeup irritation.","The rash seems to worsen after spending time in the sun.","She has had mild morning stiffness in the small joints of her hands but no significant joint swelling or pain."]},{"sid":54084,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Dermatomyositis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":54085,"type":"medications","lines":["She takes no medications."]},{"sid":54086,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":54087,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Mother: Hashimoto thyroiditis","- Maternal aunt: Rheumatoid arthritis"]},{"sid":54088,"type":"social_history","lines":["She works as a graphic designer and has had to cut back on hours due to fatigue and muscle weakness."]},{"sid":54089,"type":"ros","lines":["She denies fevers, chills, weight loss, or recent infections."]},{"sid":54090,"type":"vitals","lines":["Vital signs are normal."]},{"sid":54091,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On physical examination, she appears tired but in no acute distress.","Neurologic exam reveals symmetric weakness of the deltoids, biceps, quadriceps, and hip flexors.","Muscle strength is preserved in the distal extremities.","Her skin shows violaceous discoloration and mild periorbital edema around the eyelids, as well as erythematous, scaly plaques on the extensor surfaces of the fingers.","Joint exam reveals no synovitis.","Reflexes and sensation are intact.","The thyroid is not enlarged."]},{"sid":54092,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies reveal an elevated creatine kinase."]},{"sid":54093,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Additional autoimmune work-up is pending."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11782,"date":"2020-07-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Rheumatology","attending":"Dr. Michael Rodriguez","cc":"gradually worsening fatigue and muscle weakness","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[6832],"sections":[{"sid":54094,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Gradually worsening fatigue and muscle weakness"]},{"sid":54095,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns for rheumatology follow-up of dermatomyositis, initially diagnosed in January 2020 for a persistent hand rash and evaluated in February 2020 for progressive fatigue.","She says that over the last few months, she has had increasing difficulty rising from chairs, climbing stairs, and lifting objects overhead.","She also describes occasional burning discomfort in her shoulders and hips, which seems worse after activity.","She denies recent travel, trauma, or significant weight loss, though she has noticed more generalized tiredness and intermittent low-grade fevers."]},{"sid":54096,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Dermatomyositis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":54097,"type":"medications","lines":["She takes no regular medications"]},{"sid":54098,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":54099,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Mother: Hashimoto thyroiditis","- Maternal aunt: Rheumatoid arthritis"]},{"sid":54100,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: Occasional (1-2 drinks per month). Occupation: Graphic designer."]},{"sid":54101,"type":"vitals","lines":["Vital signs are normal"]},{"sid":54102,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, she appears tired but in no acute distress.","There is symmetric weakness of the proximal muscles in both the upper and lower extremities, but distal strength is preserved.","No joint swelling or deformity is noted."]},{"sid":54103,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory testing reveals elevated creatine kinase and aldolase"]},{"sid":54104,"type":"pathology","lines":["A muscle biopsy is obtained and shows perifascicular atrophy"]},{"sid":54105,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Electromyography demonstrates myopathic changes"]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11784,"date":"2022-01-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Rheumatology","attending":"Dr. Aisha Patel","cc":"progressive fatigue and worsening difficulty performing daily tasks over the past 3 months","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5170],"sections":[{"sid":54106,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressive fatigue and worsening difficulty performing daily tasks over the past 3 months"]},{"sid":54107,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns for follow-up of dermatomyositis initially diagnosed in January 2020 and last evaluated in July 2020 for gradually worsening fatigue and muscle weakness.","She reports that she has been struggling to lift her arms above her head to wash her hair and has had increasing trouble rising from chairs or climbing stairs.","S